\fBNAME\fR
.br
.in 4n
usilic - pager and file manager
.in 0
.sp
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
.br
.in 4n
usilic [-c|-g] [-f font] [-u usec ...] [-i pixel ...]
.br
         [file] [< file ...] [directory]
.in 0
.sp
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
.br
.in 4n
usilic works as a pager when started with standard input or regular files as arguments, and as a file manager when given a directory argument.After startup, the arguments can be checked in "Boot options" on the \fBINFO\fR screen shown by ^I (^J^I in \fBSHELL\fR).While running, the access history of files and directories is kept and can be used again the next time usilic starts.When reading this manual page in \fBHELP\fR, the ; / : keys move to the previous / next chapter.See the \fBMACRO\fR chapter below for the actual key assignments.
.br
.sp
The main notations used in this text are as follows.
.in 0
.sp
.in 7n
.in 19n
.ti 7n
